aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic_rescue.root.speaker=Rivet Cogsworth
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic_rescue.root.body=Oil in the joints… rust peeling away… systems online. Thank you. An inn, you say? I will make my way there once my bearings return.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic_rescue.root.c0=Glad you are awake. See you at the inn.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.speaker=Rivet Cogsworth
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.body=Gears spinning clean at last. If this town needs a mechanic, I am ready to work.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.fallback=Ask about metal, shops, oil, or whatever needs fixing. My tools are warm.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.greeting.0=Joints greased. Ready for the day.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.greeting.1=I can hear a loose pin from three streets over. Handy gift.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.greeting.2=Hello. Need plate, pipe, or plain advice?
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.greeting.3=Sorry if I smell like warm oil. Habit of the trade.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.hint.love.0=A clockwork heart or bronze plate would make my circuits glow.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.hint.love.1=Bring me something precise from the Expanse. Fine parts feel like home.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.hint.dislike.0=Please leave trash and dirt outside. My intakes clog easily.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.main_hub.hint.dislike.1=Junk piles are no gift. I left enough rust behind already.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_house=You wanted to talk about a house.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_house_done=Your name is on the house shelf. I wanted you to hear it from me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_house_remind=The house is still in progress.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_shop_done=I wanted to check in now that the mechanics shop is standing.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_shop_complete=The mechanics shop is finished. I am here to close things out with you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_shop_building=The shop is still coming together. I wanted to ask where things stand.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_shop_offer=I want to help you open a mechanics shop in town.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_rust=Tell me about the Rusted Expanse.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_tools=What tools do you recommend?
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_oil=Why did the oil wake you?
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.root.c_goodbye=That is all for now. See you later.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_quest_shop.body=I know metals the way fishers know tides. A proper shop would stock iron, copper, bronze, gold, zinc, and the scrap gear of my homeland. I sketched shelves for every plate and pipe. If you raise it for the town, I will share those plans.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_quest_shop.c0=We will get your shop built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_quest_shop.c1=Not right now. I need a bit more time.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_shop_accepted.body=Here are my shop plans. Study them at the town planning desk, craft a plot token when you are ready, and stake the shop where travelers can find metal. I will wait at the inn until the door is real.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_shop_accepted.c0=See you when the shelves are up.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_building.body=I keep counting the gears in my pocket while I wait. Have you learned the plans and started the build yet, or should I stop counting on a shop that might not happen?
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_building.c0=I need to drop the quest for now.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_building.c1=I am still working on it and I will keep going.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_abandoned.body=That is all right. Rust waits for no one, and neither do clocks. If you change your mind, come find me and we will try again.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_abandoned.c0=Fair enough. I will see you around.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_done.body=Hear that? Soft tick, smooth counter, honest shelves. Metal on display and scrap sorted by size. Thank you for giving a free robot a place that fits.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_done.c0=Happy to help. Come find me if the town needs more metal.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_offer.body=The shop is for work. After sleeping in rust and inn corners, I would still love a little house with a rack for spare springs and a window for rainy mornings.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_offer.c0=I will stake a house for you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_offer.c1=Another time.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_accepted.body=When the walls are up, put my name on the block inside like the charter asks, then come tell me in person. I want to hear you say it before I start moving my kit off the inn floor.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_accepted.c0=You will hear it from me.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_remind.body=Take your time with the frame. When it is standing, register me on the shelf inside, then come back. I am not rushing you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_remind.c0=Understood.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_finish.body=Oh, this is lovely. Warm light, quiet walls, and just enough room for an oil can by the door. No more sleeping under rust for me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.rivet_house_finish.c0=Glad you have a proper door.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.talk_rust.body=The Rusted Expanse still hums with old machines. Scrap, gear trees, and sleeping golems under giant heads. Bring careful feet and a sharp eye.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.talk_rust.c0=Thanks. I will keep my eyes open.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.talk_tools.body=Start with scrap and bronze plate. A mechanic's bench turns waste into bolts and clever tools. Oil keeps joints from locking again.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.talk_tools.c0=I will keep that in mind.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.talk_oil.body=Black oil slides under rust and wakes seals that sand packed shut. Throw a sealed husk into a pool and the shell softens. After I am free, more husks just melt into scrap. Fair trade.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.talk_oil.c0=That makes sense.

aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.gift.love=Now that is a gift worth waking for. Thank you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.gift.like=A fine little present. Feels like finding a matching bolt in a bin.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.gift.neutral=Hmm. I will find a use for it somehow. Mechanics learn not to waste much.
aetherhaven.dialogue.machinaria_mechanic.gift.dislike=I would rather you kept that. My intakes reject clutter.
